  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[fingerprint]` is justified.\n\n- **The claim matches the source.** `UnreadContents` is declared as `pub enum UnreadContents {}`, so it has no variants and no value of it can exist. The body `match *self {}` is an empty match on an uninhabited type. It has no executable case, so the function can never run and will show no execution coverage.\n- **The stated reason is substantive.** The commentary says the empty match only satisfies the trait bound on the `Domain` associated type. `StoredGraph`'s `Domain` impl sets `type NodeContent = UnreadContents`, and the `NodeContents` trait requires `fingerprint`. That is a structural reason, not just difficulty. It also agrees with the sibling `fn[format]` and with `StoredGraph`'s `node_content`, which panics so that no content is ever read.\n- **The form is valid.** The explanation is in fenced `:::{cite}` commentary attached to the function. This is a function-level exception, so it excuses only that function's zero execution and not the file's threshold.\n- **No redundant citation.** The item has no other `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`.",
